From aac46295711c41a4d039d07cb575462ae7ee21ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <dev@simplyluma.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:38:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] broadband-bearer-external: packet data through an
 external service

Some modems cannot bind a PDN to a net port from the AT port: MediaTek CCCI modems need their MIPC host channel for it. A primary port tagged ID_MM_AT_DATA_SERVICE=<bus name> now gets bearers that connect through that service (<name>.Data Connect/Disconnect at /<name as path>/Data) and use the net port it returns; IPv6 is configured by the network (SLAAC), IPv4 only when it was the only family asked for. Name servers the service reports (dns4/dns6, e.g. from PCO) are passed on in the bearer IP configuration.
---
